---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';
import {url} from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title="Retail Finance Platform" page="home" narrow
 description="Follow a finance request from question to trusted evidence, checked draft, human approval and controlled delivery."
 footer="Synthetic data only. This site explains a paused demonstration and a proposed enterprise design. It does not run the finance agent.">
 <h1 slot="header">A finance question. A checked answer. A human decision.</h1>
 <main><div class="wrap">
  <p class="lead">A controller asks for the month-end commentary. The agent reads trusted finance results, drafts an explanation and waits for approval. Follow that one request from start to finish.</p>
  <div class="home-request"><span class="lbl">Start with a real question</span><blockquote>“Explain the August close: revenue, margin, exceptions and the forecast.”</blockquote><a class="primary-link" href={url('architecture/architecture.html')}>Follow the request →</a></div>
  <div class="home-path"><span>Request</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><span>Check access & data</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><span>Plan & retrieve evidence</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><span>Draft & validate</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><span>Human approval</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span><span>Controlled delivery</span></div>
  <div class="cards">
   <a class="card" style="--c:var(--agent)" href={url('architecture/architecture.html#built-hld')}><h2>Understand the demonstration</h2><p>Eight stages in request order. Simple explains the story; Expert reveals the components in the same places.</p><span class="go">Explore as built →</span></a>
   <a class="card" style="--c:var(--data)" href={url('architecture/architecture.html#target-hld')}><h2>See what production adds</h2><p>The same month-end question and eight stages, with proposed production additions clearly marked.</p><span class="go">Compare the enterprise target →</span></a>
   <a class="card" style="--c:var(--base)" href={url('landscape/platform-landscape.html')}><h2>Find where a component fits</h2><p>Components appear at the stage that uses them. Credentials, hosting and monitoring sit in supporting detail.</p><span class="go">Open the platform map →</span></a>
  </div>
  <div class="facts"><div><b>Demonstrated</b>AWS + Databricks + Google; core platform built</div><div><b>Data</b>40 synthetic stores · 21 months · 4.2m rows</div><div><b>Boundary</b>No financial postings or payments; approval before delivery</div><div><b>Today</b>Paused; target is a design, not deployed functionality</div></div>
  <p class="lead">The redesign changes the explanation, not the running platform. <a href="https://github.com/kheuchi/retail-finance-platform-control-plane/blob/main/docs/architecture/hld.md">Read the architecture and implementation limits</a>, or compare <a href={url('landscape/tools.html')}>tool options</a>.</p>
 </div></main>
 <style>.home-request{background:#182b38;color:#fff;padding:28px;border-radius:12px}.home-request .lbl{color:#bfd5e0}.home-request blockquote{font:500 27px/1.4 var(--f-display);margin:12px 0 20px;max-width:700px}.primary-link{display:inline-block;padding:11px 16px;background:#fff;color:#182b38;border-radius:7px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600}.home-path{display:grid;justify-items:center;gap:7px;padding:20px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;background:var(--paper)}.home-path span:nth-child(odd){font-weight:600}.home-path span:nth-child(even){color:var(--agent)}</style>
</Base>
